var e={level:`C1`,type:`verb-conjugate`,questions:[{id:`c1-vc-001`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'No sooner' use the past perfect with inversion: had he arrived.`,wrongReasons:{"he had arrived":`After 'No sooner' the auxiliary must come before the subject.`,"did he arrive":`'No sooner' is followed by the past perfect: had he arrived.`},text:`No sooner ___ (he / arrive) than it began to rain.`,answers:[[`had he arrived`]]},{id:`c1-vc-002`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'I'd rather' + a new subject, use the past simple: I'd rather you didn't tell.`,wrongReasons:{"don't tell":`After 'I'd rather' + subject, use the past simple.`,"wouldn't tell":`'would' is not used after 'I'd rather' + subject.`},text:`I'd rather you ___ (not / tell) anyone.`,answers:[[`didn't tell`,`did not tell`]]},{id:`c1-vc-003`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle clause has a passive meaning: Built in 1900, the house needs repairs.`,wrongReasons:{writing:`The guide is written by someone, so a passive participle is needed.`,"having written":`'Having written' is active and means the guide wrote something.`},text:`___ (write) in simple language, the guide is ideal for beginners.`,answers:[[`Written`]]},{id:`c1-vc-004`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Never before' at the start, invert the auxiliary and subject: Never before had she felt so happy.`,wrongReasons:{"i had seen":`After 'Never before' the auxiliary must come before the subject.`,"i have seen":`The word order must be inverted: 'have I seen'.`},text:`Never before ___ (I / see) such a breathtaking sunset.`,answers:[[`had I seen`,`have I seen`]]},{id:`c1-vc-005`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Wish + past perfect expresses regret about the past: He wishes he had travelled more.`,wrongReasons:{studied:`The regret is about the past ('when she was younger'), so use the past perfect.`,"would study":`'would' cannot express regret about the past.`},text:`Lisa wishes she ___ (study) medicine instead of law when she was younger.`,answers:[[`had studied`]]},{id:`c1-vc-006`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'advise that' use the bare subjunctive or should + infinitive: She advised that he rest.`,wrongReasons:{avoids:`The subjunctive has no -s ending.`,avoided:`After 'advised that' the subjunctive uses the base form, not the past.`},text:`The doctor advised that he ___ (avoid) salt for a few weeks.`,answers:[[`avoid`,`should avoid`]]},{id:`c1-vc-007`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an action completed before a future time, use the future perfect passive: By June, the work will have been finished.`,wrongReasons:{"will have replaced":`The cars do not replace anything; a passive form is needed.`,"have been replaced":`2030 is in the future, so the present perfect is wrong.`},text:`By 2030, most petrol cars ___ (replace) by electric ones.`,answers:[[`will have been replaced`,`will be replaced`]]},{id:`c1-vc-008`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'recommend that' use the bare subjunctive (or should + infinitive): They recommended that he leave.`,wrongReasons:{resigns:`After 'recommend that' the subjunctive has no -s ending.`,resigned:`The subjunctive uses the base form, not the past simple.`},text:`The committee recommended that the chairman ___ (resign) immediately.`,answers:[[`resign`,`should resign`]]},{id:`c1-vc-009`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For regret about the past, use wish + past perfect: I wish I had studied more.`,wrongReasons:{"didn't say":`'yesterday' shows a past regret, so use the past perfect.`,"wouldn't have said":`After 'I wish I', past regret is expressed with the past perfect, not 'would have'.`},text:`I wish I ___ (not / say) such hurtful things to her yesterday.`,answers:[[`hadn't said`,`had not said`]]},{id:`c1-vc-010`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A present participle can replace an active relative clause: the smell coming (= which was coming) from the kitchen.`,wrongReasons:{came:`The sentence already has a main verb, so use the participle 'coming'.`,comes:`Without 'which', a finite verb cannot follow 'noise'.`},text:`The noise ___ (come) from the basement turned out to be a broken pipe.`,answers:[[`coming`]]},{id:`c1-vc-011`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Only after' + clause, invert in the main clause: Only after he left did I understand.`,wrongReasons:{"the scientists realised":`After 'Only after ...' the main clause needs inversion with 'did'.`,"realised the scientists":`Use 'did' + subject + base verb, not the main verb before the subject.`},text:`Only after the results were published ___ (the scientists / realise) their mistake.`,answers:[[`did the scientists realise`,`did the scientists realize`]]},{id:`c1-vc-012`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'have something done' uses the past participle: I had my hair cut.`,wrongReasons:{service:`After 'have + object' use the past participle, not the base form.`,"to service":`The causative 'have something done' does not take a to-infinitive.`},text:`I'm having my car ___ (service) tomorrow morning.`,answers:[[`serviced`]]},{id:`c1-vc-013`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'propose that' use the subjunctive; in the passive this is 'be' + past participle: I propose that it be cancelled.`,wrongReasons:{"is postponed":`After 'propose that' use the subjunctive 'be postponed'.`,postpone:`The meeting does not postpone anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`I propose that the meeting ___ (postpone) until next week.`,answers:[[`be postponed`,`should be postponed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-014`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A negative passive participle clause can be 'Not having been' + past participle: Not having been told, I was surprised.`,wrongReasons:{"not been":`'Not been' is incomplete; use 'Not having been'.`,"not having":`The passive needs 'been': 'Not having been invited'.`},text:`___ (not / be) invited to the wedding, they felt deeply offended.`,answers:[[`Not having been`,`Not being`]]},{id:`c1-vc-015`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'All things considered' is a fixed absolute participle phrase meaning 'taking everything into account'.`,wrongReasons:{considering:`The fixed expression is 'all things considered', with the past participle.`,consider:`The base form cannot be used; use 'considered'.`},text:`All things ___ (consider), the trip was a success.`,answers:[[`considered`]]},{id:`c1-vc-016`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use the perfect participle for an action that happened first and caused the next: Having missed the bus, I walked.`,wrongReasons:{losing:`He lost the keys before climbing in, so use 'Having lost'.`,lost:`'Lost' alone gives a passive meaning; use 'Having lost'.`},text:`___ (lose) his keys, he had to climb in through the window.`,answers:[[`Having lost`]]},{id:`c1-vc-017`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Third conditional: if + past perfect, would have + past participle: What would you have said if he had asked?`,wrongReasons:{refused:`The question is about the past, so the if-clause needs the past perfect.`,"would have refused":`'would have' belongs in the result clause, not in the if-clause.`},text:`What would you have done if the bank ___ (refuse) your loan application?`,answers:[[`had refused`]]},{id:`c1-vc-018`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a past passive action after 'is thought', use to have been + past participle: It is believed to have been built in 1200.`,wrongReasons:{"to be written":`The writing happened in the past, so use the perfect passive infinitive.`,"to have written":`The manuscript did not write anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`The ancient manuscript is thought ___ (write) by monks in the ninth century.`,answers:[[`to have been written`]]},{id:`c1-vc-019`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use wish + would to complain about someone else's annoying habit: I wish he would stop shouting.`,wrongReasons:{stop:`After 'I wish' the present simple is not used.`,"will stop":`After 'wish' use 'would', not 'will'.`},text:`I wish my neighbours ___ (stop) playing loud music every night.`,answers:[[`would stop`,`stopped`]]},{id:`c1-vc-020`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'It's about time' + subject takes the past simple: It's about time we left.`,wrongReasons:{start:`After 'It's about time' + subject, use the past simple.`,"have started":`The present perfect does not follow 'It's about time' + subject.`},text:`It's about time you ___ (start) taking your studies seriously.`,answers:[[`started`]]},{id:`c1-vc-021`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A present participle can show an action immediately before the main one: Opening the door, she saw him.`,wrongReasons:{turned:`'Turned' gives a passive meaning; use 'Turning'.`,"to turn":`A to-infinitive here would express purpose, which does not fit.`},text:`___ (turn) the corner, we saw the cathedral rising above the rooftops.`,answers:[[`Turning`,`Having turned`]]},{id:`c1-vc-022`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle clause has a passive meaning: Told the news, he cried.`,wrongReasons:{informing:`The passengers received the information, so a passive form is needed.`,"having informed":`'Having informed' is active and means the passengers informed someone.`},text:`___ (inform) of the delay, the passengers began to complain.`,answers:[[`Informed`,`Having been informed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-023`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'The reason why ... is/was that' focuses on a cause: The reason he failed was that he didn't study.`,wrongReasons:{were:`'The reason' is singular, so 'were' is wrong.`,are:`'The reason' is singular, so use 'is' or 'was'.`},text:`The reason why I left ___ (be) that I felt undervalued.`,answers:[[`was`,`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-024`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'for the past six months' needs the present perfect passive: The road has been blocked for weeks.`,wrongReasons:{"is closed":`A period continuing until now needs the present perfect.`,"was closed":`The closure continues until now, so the past simple is wrong.`},text:`The museum ___ (close) for renovation for the past six months.`,answers:[[`has been closed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-025`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'In no way' invert the verb 'be' and the subject: In no way was she to blame.`,wrongReasons:{"i was":`After 'In no way' at the start, the verb must come before the subject.`,"i am":`Inversion is required: put the verb before 'I'.`},text:`In no way ___ (I / be) responsible for the accident yesterday.`,answers:[[`was I`,`am I`]]},{id:`c1-vc-026`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional: past condition, present result with would + infinitive: If I had moved, I would live there now.`,wrongReasons:{"would have lived":`'now' shows a present result, so use would + infinitive, not would have + past participle.`,"will live":`This is an imaginary situation, so 'will' is wrong; use 'would'.`},text:`If she had accepted the post in Tokyo, she ___ (live) in Japan now.`,answers:[[`would be living`,`would live`]]},{id:`c1-vc-027`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'since' needs the present perfect passive: No letters have been sent since Monday.`,wrongReasons:{"was received":`'since' requires the present perfect, not the past simple.`,"has received":`A complaint does not receive anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`Not a single complaint ___ (receive) since the new system was introduced.`,answers:[[`has been received`]]},{id:`c1-vc-028`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an action completed before another past action, use the past perfect passive: The cake had already been eaten.`,wrongReasons:{"were already stolen":`The theft happened before the police arrived, so use the past perfect passive.`,"had already stolen":`The jewels did not steal anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`By the time the police arrived, the jewels ___ (already / steal).`,answers:[[`had already been stolen`]]},{id:`c1-vc-029`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a past action after 'is believed', use the perfect infinitive: He is thought to have escaped.`,wrongReasons:{"to leave":`'last week' refers to the past, so use the perfect infinitive.`,leaving:`After 'is believed' use an infinitive, not the -ing form.`},text:`The suspect is believed ___ (leave) the country last week.`,answers:[[`to have left`]]},{id:`c1-vc-030`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A present participle can replace 'who + verb': Anyone needing help (= who needs help) should ask.`,wrongReasons:{wishes:`Without 'who', a finite verb cannot follow 'Anyone' here.`,wished:`The past participle gives a passive meaning, which does not fit.`},text:`Anyone ___ (wish) to attend the workshop should register online.`,answers:[[`wishing`]]},{id:`c1-vc-031`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`To give advice use 'If I were you' + would: If I were you, I would wait.`,wrongReasons:{am:`Advice with 'would' needs the unreal past, not the present.`,"had been":`The advice is about now, not about the past.`},text:`If I ___ (be) you, I would get a second opinion before signing the contract.`,answers:[[`were`,`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-032`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'The thing that ... was' is a cleft-like structure with a singular verb: The thing I liked was the food.`,wrongReasons:{were:`'The thing' is singular, so use 'was'.`,is:`The experience is in the past ('surprised'), so use 'was'.`},text:`The thing that surprised me most ___ (be) how friendly everyone was.`,answers:[[`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-033`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an unreal past condition use the past perfect: If I had known, I would have gone.`,wrongReasons:{knew:`The result 'would have taken' is in the past, so the if-clause needs the past perfect, not the past simple.`,"would have known":`'would' is not normally used in the if-clause; use the past perfect.`},text:`If I ___ (know) about the strike, I would have taken a taxi to the airport.`,answers:[[`had known`]]},{id:`c1-vc-034`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A present participle can show an action happening at the same time: He left, waving goodbye.`,wrongReasons:{slammed:`After the comma, a participle is needed for the simultaneous action, not the past simple.`,"having slammed":`The perfect participle suggests the slam happened before she walked out.`},text:`She walked out of the room, ___ (slam) the door behind her.`,answers:[[`slamming`]]},{id:`c1-vc-035`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle clause gives passive background information: Founded in 1850, the school is famous.`,wrongReasons:{completing:`The tower was completed by builders, so a passive participle is needed.`,"having completed":`'Having completed' is active and would mean the tower completed something.`},text:`___ (complete) in 1889, the tower was initially criticised by many artists.`,answers:[[`Completed`,`Having been completed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-036`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'It was only after ... that' is followed by the past simple: It was only after she left that I understood.`,wrongReasons:{"has taken up":`'It was' places the event in the past, so the present perfect is wrong.`,"takes up":`The event is in the past, so use the past simple.`},text:`It was only after he had retired that he ___ (take up) painting.`,answers:[[`took up`]]},{id:`c1-vc-037`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'At no time' invert the auxiliary and subject: At no time did he apologise.`,wrongReasons:{"the company informed":`After 'At no time' at the start, invert with 'did'.`,"informed the company":`Use 'did' + subject + base form, not the main verb before the subject.`},text:`At no time ___ (the company / inform) its customers of the risk.`,answers:[[`did the company inform`,`had the company informed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-038`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional with a present result: If you had studied, you wouldn't have problems now.`,wrongReasons:{"wouldn't have had":`'now' shows a present result, so use would + infinitive.`,"won't have":`The situation is imaginary, so 'will' is wrong.`},text:`If you had listened to my advice, you ___ (not / have) this problem now.`,answers:[[`wouldn't have`,`would not have`]]},{id:`c1-vc-039`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'unless' use a present tense to talk about the future: Unless it rains, we will go.`,wrongReasons:{"will approve":`After 'unless' use a present tense for the future, not 'will'.`,"doesn't approve":`'Unless' already means 'if not', so a negative verb gives the opposite meaning.`},text:`Unless the board ___ (approve) the budget by Friday, the project will be postponed.`,answers:[[`approves`,`approve`]]},{id:`c1-vc-040`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'It is imperative that' use the bare subjunctive: It is imperative that he be told.`,wrongReasons:{takes:`The subjunctive uses the base form without -s.`,took:`The past simple is wrong after 'It is imperative that'.`},text:`It is imperative that the patient ___ (take) the medication at the same time every day.`,answers:[[`take`,`should take`]]},{id:`c1-vc-041`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'would rather' + another subject, use the past simple: I'd rather you stayed.`,wrongReasons:{spend:`After 'would rather' + a different subject, use the past simple.`,"would spend":`'would' is not repeated after 'would rather' + subject.`},text:`My parents would rather we ___ (spend) Christmas with them this year.`,answers:[[`spent`]]},{id:`c1-vc-042`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A what-clause takes a singular verb: What worries me is the cost.`,wrongReasons:{are:`The what-clause and 'the way' are singular, so use 'is'.`,annoys:`The verb 'annoys' is already in the what-clause; the gap needs 'be'.`},text:`What really annoys me ___ (be) the way he ignores everyone.`,answers:[[`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-043`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Such + be + noun + that' is an inverted structure: Such was his anger that he shouted.`,wrongReasons:{is:`The story is in the past (the website crashed), so use 'was'.`,were:`'demand' is singular, so use 'was'.`},text:`Such ___ (be) the demand for tickets that the website crashed.`,answers:[[`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-044`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Being' can give a reason: Being tired, she went to bed early.`,wrongReasons:{been:`'Been' cannot start a participle clause on its own.`,"having been":`'Having been' suggests he is no longer a vegetarian, which contradicts 'never orders'.`},text:`___ (be) a vegetarian, he never orders the meat dishes.`,answers:[[`Being`]]},{id:`c1-vc-045`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a demand after 'insist that', use the subjunctive 'be': He insisted that the door be locked.`,wrongReasons:{was:`'was' would mean she claimed the lawyer was there; for a demand use 'be'.`,is:`After a past 'insisted that' expressing a demand, use the subjunctive 'be'.`},text:`She insisted that her lawyer ___ (be) present during the interview.`,answers:[[`be`,`should be`]]},{id:`c1-vc-046`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Only by' + -ing, invert the auxiliary and subject: Only by saving can you buy a house.`,wrongReasons:{"we can solve":`After 'Only by ...' at the start, the auxiliary comes before the subject.`,"we solve":`An auxiliary is needed for inversion: 'can we solve'.`},text:`Only by working together ___ (we / solve) this problem.`,answers:[[`can we solve`,`will we solve`]]},{id:`c1-vc-047`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`An inverted third conditional uses Had + subject + past participle: Had I known, I would have come.`,wrongReasons:{"i realise":`After 'Had' use the past participle 'realised'.`,"i had realised":`'Had' is already at the start; do not repeat it.`},text:`Had ___ (I / realise) how late it was, I would have called a taxi.`,answers:[[`I realised`,`I realized`]]},{id:`c1-vc-048`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Generally speaking' is a fixed participle expression meaning 'in general': Generally speaking, it is safe.`,wrongReasons:{spoken:`The fixed expression uses the present participle: 'generally speaking'.`,speak:`The base form cannot be used here; use 'speaking'.`},text:`Generally ___ (speak), older cars use more fuel than newer models.`,answers:[[`speaking`]]},{id:`c1-vc-049`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'It was + place + that' focuses on where; the clause uses the past simple: It was in Paris that they met.`,wrongReasons:{"has composed":`Mozart's life is finished, so the present perfect is wrong.`,composes:`The event is in the past, so use the past simple.`},text:`It was in Vienna that Mozart ___ (compose) many of his greatest works.`,answers:[[`composed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-050`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'I'd sooner' + another subject works like 'I'd rather' and takes the past simple: I'd sooner you came early.`,wrongReasons:{pay:`After 'I'd sooner' + a different subject, use the past simple.`,"would pay":`'would' is not used after 'I'd sooner' + subject.`},text:`I'd sooner you ___ (pay) me in cash, if that's all right.`,answers:[[`paid`]]},{id:`c1-vc-051`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'What ... did was', use the bare infinitive (or to-infinitive): What I did was call him.`,wrongReasons:{cutting:`After 'What ... did was' use the infinitive, not the -ing form.`,cuts:`After 'was' in this structure use the base form, not the present simple.`},text:`What the company did was ___ (cut) the budget by half.`,answers:[[`cut`,`to cut`]]},{id:`c1-vc-052`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Should' + subject in a formal condition, use the bare infinitive: Should you need help, call us.`,wrongReasons:{arrives:`After 'Should' + subject, use the bare infinitive without -s.`,arrived:`'Should' is always followed by the bare infinitive.`},text:`Should the shipment ___ (arrive) damaged, please contact us within 48 hours.`,answers:[[`arrive`]]},{id:`c1-vc-053`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Only when' + clause, invert the main clause: Only when I saw it did I believe it.`,wrongReasons:{"she understood":`After 'Only when ...' the main clause needs inversion with 'did'.`,"understood she":`Use 'did' + subject + base form for inversion.`},text:`Only when she read the letter again ___ (she / understand) what he meant.`,answers:[[`did she understand`]]},{id:`c1-vc-054`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Under no circumstances' invert the auxiliary and subject: Under no circumstances is smoking permitted.`,wrongReasons:{"visitors are allowed":`After a negative phrase at the start, invert: 'are visitors allowed'.`,"are allowed visitors":`Only the auxiliary moves before the subject; the participle stays after it.`},text:`Under no circumstances ___ (visitors / allow) to feed the animals.`,answers:[[`are visitors allowed`,`will visitors be allowed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-055`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`The negative passive subjunctive is 'not be' + past participle: It is vital that it not be lost.`,wrongReasons:{"is not shared":`After 'It is vital that' use the subjunctive 'not be shared', not the indicative.`,"not share":`The data does not share anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`It is vital that the data ___ (not / share) with third parties.`,answers:[[`not be shared`,`should not be shared`,`shouldn't be shared`]]},{id:`c1-vc-056`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'is reported', use the continuous infinitive for an action in progress: He is said to be living abroad.`,wrongReasons:{training:`After 'is reported' use an infinitive, not the -ing form.`,"to have trained":`The training is still going on, so a continuous infinitive is needed.`},text:`The athlete is reported ___ (train) in secret for the next Olympics.`,answers:[[`to be training`,`to have been training`]]},{id:`c1-vc-057`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Provided that' introduces a real condition and takes a present tense for the future: Provided that you pay, you can enter.`,wrongReasons:{"will hold":`Do not use 'will' after 'provided that'; use the present simple.`,held:`This is a real future condition, so the past simple is wrong here.`},text:`Provided that the weather ___ (hold), the ceremony will take place outdoors.`,answers:[[`holds`]]},{id:`c1-vc-058`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'If only' + past perfect expresses regret about the past: If only I had known.`,wrongReasons:{listened:`The regret is about a past event, so use the past perfect.`,"would listen":`'would' expresses a wish for change, not regret about the past.`},text:`If only they ___ (listen) to the engineers before building the dam!`,answers:[[`had listened`]]},{id:`c1-vc-059`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional: present state, past result with would have + past participle: If he were kinder, he would have helped.`,wrongReasons:{"would apologise":`'long ago' refers to the past, so the result needs would have + past participle.`,"had apologised":`The result clause needs 'would have', not the past perfect alone.`},text:`If he weren't so stubborn, he ___ (apologise) to his sister long ago.`,answers:[[`would have apologised`,`would have apologized`]]},{id:`c1-vc-060`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Hardly ... when' takes the past perfect with inversion: Hardly had I left when it started.`,wrongReasons:{"we had sat":`After 'Hardly' at the start, the auxiliary comes before the subject.`,"did we sit":`'Hardly ... when' is followed by the past perfect, not the past simple.`},text:`Hardly ___ (we / sit) down when the phone rang.`,answers:[[`had we sat`]]},{id:`c1-vc-061`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use 'Having' + past participle for an action completed before the main one: Having eaten, we left.`,wrongReasons:{finished:`Without 'having', the participle has a passive meaning, which does not fit.`,finishing:`The report was finished before it was sent, so use the perfect participle.`},text:`___ (finish) the report, she sent it to her manager.`,answers:[[`Having finished`]]},{id:`c1-vc-062`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In a what-cleft, the focused clause keeps its normal tense: What I wonder is why he left.`,wrongReasons:{"has resigned":`'last month' is a finished time, so the present perfect is wrong.`,resigns:`The event is in the past, so use the past simple.`},text:`What I can't understand is why she ___ (resign) so suddenly last month.`,answers:[[`resigned`]]},{id:`c1-vc-063`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'make' takes the bare infinitive in the active, but the to-infinitive in the passive: He was made to wait.`,wrongReasons:{work:`In the passive, 'be made' is followed by the to-infinitive.`,working:`'be made' is not followed by the -ing form.`},text:`The prisoners were made ___ (work) twelve hours a day.`,answers:[[`to work`]]},{id:`c1-vc-064`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'What I'm going to do is' use the bare infinitive (or to-infinitive): What I'll do is call her.`,wrongReasons:{writing:`After 'What ... do is' use the infinitive, not the -ing form.`,wrote:`The plan is for the future, so the past simple is wrong.`},text:`What I'm going to do is ___ (write) a formal complaint.`,answers:[[`write`,`to write`]]},{id:`c1-vc-065`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Would you rather' + another subject takes the past simple: Would you rather I stayed?`,wrongReasons:{come:`After 'would rather' + a different subject, use the past simple.`,"would come":`'would' is not repeated after 'would rather' + subject.`},text:`Would you rather I ___ (come) with you to the hospital?`,answers:[[`came`]]},{id:`c1-vc-066`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Were + subject + to-infinitive' is a formal unreal condition: Were he to resign, there would be chaos.`,wrongReasons:{collapsed:`After 'Were the company' use the to-infinitive, not the past simple.`,collapse:`The infinitive needs 'to' in this structure.`},text:`Were the company ___ (collapse), thousands of jobs would be lost.`,answers:[[`to collapse`]]},{id:`c1-vc-067`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'On no account' invert the modal and subject: On no account should you leave.`,wrongReasons:{"you should open":`After 'On no account' at the start, the modal comes before the subject.`,"you open":`Inversion needs an auxiliary or modal before the subject.`},text:`On no account ___ (you / open) this door without permission.`,answers:[[`should you open`,`must you open`]]},{id:`c1-vc-068`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Rarely' at the start, invert the auxiliary and subject: Rarely have I seen such talent.`,wrongReasons:{"the committee has rejected":`After 'Rarely' at the start, the auxiliary must come before the subject.`,"did the committee rejected":`After 'did' use the base form, and here the present perfect is needed.`},text:`Rarely ___ (the committee / reject) a proposal as firmly as it did yesterday.`,answers:[[`has the committee rejected`]]},{id:`c1-vc-069`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In an 'It is ... who' cleft, the verb agrees with the focused noun: It is the parents who pay.`,wrongReasons:{decides:`'the students' is plural, so the verb has no -s.`,deciding:`The relative clause needs a finite verb.`},text:`It is the students themselves who ___ (decide) which topics to study.`,answers:[[`decide`]]},{id:`c1-vc-070`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Suppose' + past simple introduces an imaginary situation with 'would': Suppose it rained, would you come?`,wrongReasons:{finds:`The question uses 'would', so the condition needs the past simple.`,"had found":`The past perfect refers to the past, but this is an imaginary future.`},text:`Suppose the manager ___ (find) out. What would you say?`,answers:[[`found`,`were to find`]]},{id:`c1-vc-071`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'need', use the passive infinitive (or -ing) when the subject receives the action: The walls need to be painted.`,wrongReasons:{"to sign":`The documents do not sign anything; use 'to be signed'.`,"to signed":`After 'to' use 'be' + past participle, not the participle alone.`},text:`All the documents need ___ (sign) before the end of the day.`,answers:[[`to be signed`,`signing`]]},{id:`c1-vc-072`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`The passive subjunctive is 'be' + past participle: They demand that the law be changed.`,wrongReasons:{"are raised":`After 'demand that' use the subjunctive 'be raised', not 'are'.`,raise:`Wages do not raise anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`The union is demanding that wages ___ (raise) by five per cent.`,answers:[[`be raised`,`should be raised`]]},{id:`c1-vc-073`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle can replace 'who are + past participle': The people invited (= who are invited) will come.`,wrongReasons:{selecting:`The students are chosen by others, so use the past participle.`,"who selected":`'who selected' means the students chose someone; a passive meaning is needed.`},text:`The students ___ (select) for the programme will spend a term in Canada.`,answers:[[`selected`]]},{id:`c1-vc-074`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'is expected', use the passive infinitive when the subject receives the action: The bill is expected to be approved.`,wrongReasons:{"to settle":`The dispute does not settle anything itself here; use the passive infinitive.`,settling:`After 'is expected' use an infinitive, not the -ing form.`},text:`The dispute is expected ___ (settle) out of court.`,answers:[[`to be settled`]]},{id:`c1-vc-075`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In negative participle clauses 'not' comes before the participle: Not wanting to wait, she left.`,wrongReasons:{"knowing not":`'not' must come before the participle.`,"not known":`The past participle gives a passive meaning, which does not fit.`},text:`___ (not / know) what to say, he remained silent.`,answers:[[`Not knowing`]]},{id:`c1-vc-076`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use 'Having' + past participle for an earlier action that explains the result: Having broken his leg, he couldn't play.`,wrongReasons:{spending:`The spending happened before she had nothing left, so use the perfect participle.`,spent:`'Spent' alone gives a passive meaning; use 'Having spent'.`},text:`___ (spend) all her money on the first day, she had nothing left for souvenirs.`,answers:[[`Having spent`]]},{id:`c1-vc-077`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'As long as' introduces a condition and takes a present tense: As long as you're careful, you'll be fine.`,wrongReasons:{"will keep":`Do not use 'will' after 'as long as'.`,kept:`This is a real condition about the future, so the present simple is needed.`},text:`As long as you ___ (keep) the receipt, you can return the item within thirty days.`,answers:[[`keep`]]},{id:`c1-vc-078`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A present participle can replace a relative clause: The girl sitting there is Ann (= who is sitting).`,wrongReasons:{stands:`Without 'who', a finite verb cannot follow; use 'standing'.`,stand:`The base form cannot shorten a relative clause; use the -ing form.`},text:`The man ___ (stand) by the window is my uncle.`,answers:[[`standing`]]},{id:`c1-vc-079`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In an 'It is ... that' cleft, the verb agrees with the focused noun: It is the views that attract visitors.`,wrongReasons:{makes:`'these small details' is plural, so the verb has no -s.`,making:`The relative clause needs a finite verb.`},text:`It is these small details that ___ (make) the hotel special.`,answers:[[`make`]]},{id:`c1-vc-080`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In a past 'What ... did' cleft, use 'was' + infinitive: What he did was (to) leave.`,wrongReasons:{is:`The action happened in the past, so use 'was'.`,were:`A what-clause is singular, so use 'was'.`},text:`What she did next ___ (be) to call the police.`,answers:[[`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-081`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'All that remains is + to-infinitive' focuses on the last action: All that remains is to sign.`,wrongReasons:{are:`'All that remains' is singular, so use 'is'.`,remains:`'remains' is already used; the gap needs the verb 'be'.`},text:`All that remains ___ (be) to thank our sponsors.`,answers:[[`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-082`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'It's time' + subject takes the past simple: It's time we went home.`,wrongReasons:{leave:`After 'It's time' + subject, use the past simple.`,"have left":`The present perfect does not follow 'It's time' + subject.`},text:`It's time we ___ (leave): the last bus goes in ten minutes.`,answers:[[`left`,`were leaving`]]},{id:`c1-vc-083`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Since' needs the present perfect; in the passive this is have been + past participle: Many trees have been planted since May.`,wrongReasons:{"were built":`'Since' requires the present perfect, not the past simple.`,"have built":`The homes did not build anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`Since the reform, thousands of new homes ___ (build) in the region.`,answers:[[`have been built`]]},{id:`c1-vc-084`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Judging by/from' is a fixed participle expression meaning 'based on': Judging by his face, he was angry.`,wrongReasons:{judged:`The fixed expression uses the present participle: 'judging by'.`,judge:`The base form cannot start this clause; use 'Judging'.`},text:`___ (judge) by the clouds, it's going to rain this afternoon.`,answers:[[`Judging`]]},{id:`c1-vc-085`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'hate', use being + past participle for a passive meaning: I hate being ignored.`,wrongReasons:{telling:`She receives the instructions, so a passive form is needed.`,"to tell":`The active infinitive means she tells others; use 'being told'.`},text:`She hates ___ (tell) what to do by her colleagues.`,answers:[[`being told`,`to be told`]]},{id:`c1-vc-086`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use wish + would (not) to complain about someone's habit: I wish you wouldn't shout.`,wrongReasons:{"don't interrupt":`After 'wish' the present simple is not used.`,"won't interrupt":`After 'wish' use 'would', not 'will'.`},text:`I wish you ___ (not / interrupt) me all the time. It's really annoying.`,answers:[[`wouldn't interrupt`,`would not interrupt`,`didn't interrupt`,`did not interrupt`]]},{id:`c1-vc-087`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A 'Where' clause can be the subject of a cleft and takes a singular verb: Where he failed was in planning.`,wrongReasons:{were:`The where-clause is singular, so use 'was'.`,is:`The mistake happened in the past ('went wrong'), so use 'was'.`},text:`Where we went wrong ___ (be) in underestimating the costs.`,answers:[[`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-088`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an action happening now, use the present continuous passive: Your order is being prepared.`,wrongReasons:{"is processing":`The application does not process anything; a passive form is needed.`,processes:`The active present simple is wrong; use 'is being processed'.`},text:`Your application ___ (process) right now, so please do not submit it again.`,answers:[[`is being processed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-089`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a passive action in progress in the past, use was/were being + past participle: The room was being cleaned when I arrived.`,wrongReasons:{"were discussed":`The discussion was in progress when the alarm went off, so use the continuous passive.`,"had discussed":`The proposals did not discuss anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`The proposals ___ (discuss) when the fire alarm went off.`,answers:[[`were being discussed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-090`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'It is essential that' use the bare subjunctive: It is essential that she arrive on time.`,wrongReasons:{wears:`The subjunctive does not take -s, even with a singular subject.`,wore:`After 'It is essential that' use the base form, not the past.`},text:`It is essential that every passenger ___ (wear) a seat belt during take-off.`,answers:[[`wear`,`should wear`]]},{id:`c1-vc-091`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle can shorten a passive relative clause: The cars made here (= which are made) are sold abroad.`,wrongReasons:{exporting:`The goods receive the action, so use the past participle.`,"are exported":`The sentence already has a main verb, so a finite verb cannot be added here.`},text:`Most of the goods ___ (export) to Asia come from this port.`,answers:[[`exported`]]},{id:`c1-vc-092`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Only then' at the start, invert with an auxiliary: Only then did we realise.`,wrongReasons:{"the truth became":`After 'Only then' at the start, the main clause needs inversion with 'did'.`,"became the truth":`A main verb cannot move before the subject here; use 'did'.`},text:`Only then ___ (the truth / become) clear to the investigators.`,answers:[[`did the truth become`]]},{id:`c1-vc-093`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a deduction about the past in the passive, use must have been + past participle: It must have been stolen.`,wrongReasons:{"be damaged":`The damage happened in the past, so use 'have been damaged'.`,"have damaged":`The painting did not damage anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`The painting must ___ (damage) during transport, as it was fine when it left the gallery.`,answers:[[`have been damaged`]]},{id:`c1-vc-094`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'On condition that' is followed by a present tense for the future: on condition that you return it.`,wrongReasons:{"will bring":`Do not use 'will' after 'on condition that'.`,"would bring":`The main clause uses 'will', so this is a real condition; 'would' does not fit.`},text:`I'll lend you the car on condition that you ___ (bring) it back by midnight.`,answers:[[`bring`]]},{id:`c1-vc-095`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle can replace a passive relative clause: the points made (= which were made).`,wrongReasons:{raising:`The issues were raised by people, so a passive participle is needed.`,rose:`'rise' is intransitive; the correct verb is 'raise', past participle 'raised'.`},text:`There were several issues ___ (raise) at the meeting that need further discussion.`,answers:[[`raised`]]},{id:`c1-vc-096`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a finished past action in the passive, use was/were + past participle: The letter was found in 1990.`,wrongReasons:{discovered:`The ruins did not discover anything; a passive form is needed.`,"have been discovered":`'in 1947' is a finished time, so the present perfect is wrong.`},text:`The ruins ___ (discover) by a shepherd in 1947.`,answers:[[`were discovered`]]},{id:`c1-vc-097`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A what-clause takes a singular verb: What the data suggests is that prices will rise.`,wrongReasons:{are:`The what-clause is singular, so use 'is'.`,shows:`The verb 'shows' is already in the what-clause; the gap needs 'be'.`},text:`What the report shows ___ (be) that the policy has failed.`,answers:[[`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-098`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'require that' use the bare subjunctive: The law requires that he register.`,wrongReasons:{submits:`The subjunctive has no -s ending.`,submitted:`The base form is needed after 'require that', not the past.`},text:`The regulations require that each applicant ___ (submit) two references.`,answers:[[`submit`,`should submit`]]},{id:`c1-vc-099`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In 'It wasn't ... who' clefts, use the past simple for a past event: It wasn't Sam who lied.`,wrongReasons:{breaked:`'break' is irregular: the past simple is 'broke'.`,broken:`'broken' is the past participle; the past simple 'broke' is needed.`},text:`It wasn't me who ___ (break) the vase. It was the cat!`,answers:[[`broke`]]},{id:`c1-vc-100`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle clause can add passive information: The novel, set in Rome, is a bestseller.`,wrongReasons:{basing:`The film is based on the story, so a passive participle is needed.`,"is based":`A finite verb cannot be used in this reduced clause between commas.`},text:`The film, ___ (base) on a true story, won three awards.`,answers:[[`based`]]},{id:`c1-vc-101`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Little' at the start means 'not at all' and needs inversion: Little did they suspect.`,wrongReasons:{"he knew":`After 'Little' at the start, invert with 'did'.`,"knew he":`Use the auxiliary 'did', not the main verb, before the subject.`},text:`Little ___ (he / know) that his life was about to change forever.`,answers:[[`did he know`]]},{id:`c1-vc-102`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Nowhere' at the start, invert the auxiliary and subject: Nowhere can you buy cheaper fruit.`,wrongReasons:{"you will find":`After 'Nowhere' at the start, the auxiliary comes before the subject.`,"you find":`Inversion needs an auxiliary: 'will you find'.`},text:`Nowhere ___ (you / find) a better view of the city than from this hill.`,answers:[[`will you find`,`can you find`,`could you find`]]},{id:`c1-vc-103`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional: past cause, present result: If I had saved, I wouldn't be poor now.`,wrongReasons:{"wouldn't have been":`'now' shows a present result, so use would + infinitive.`,"won't be":`The situation is imaginary, so 'will' cannot be used.`},text:`If he had been more careful with his savings, he ___ (not / be) in debt now.`,answers:[[`wouldn't be`,`would not be`]]},{id:`c1-vc-104`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In an 'It's ... that' cleft, the verb agrees with the focused noun: It's the children who need help.`,wrongReasons:{bother:`'the noise' is singular, so the verb needs -s.`,bothering:`The relative clause needs a finite verb.`},text:`It's the noise that ___ (bother) me, not the heat.`,answers:[[`bothers`]]},{id:`c1-vc-105`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Given' + noun can mean 'if I were given': Given more time, we could finish.`,wrongReasons:{giving:`The speaker would receive the chance, so use the past participle.`,"having given":`'Having given' is active and means the speaker gave something.`},text:`___ (give) the chance, I would study astrophysics.`,answers:[[`Given`]]},{id:`c1-vc-106`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'No sooner ... than' takes the past perfect with inversion: No sooner had she sat down than he arrived.`,wrongReasons:{"the guests had left":`After 'No sooner' at the start, the auxiliary comes before the subject.`,"did the guests leave":`'No sooner ... than' is normally followed by the past perfect.`},text:`No sooner ___ (the guests / leave) than the argument started again.`,answers:[[`had the guests left`]]},{id:`c1-vc-107`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use 'as though' + past simple for something that is not true: She acts as though she were the boss.`,wrongReasons:{is:`He is not the director, so use the unreal past.`,"had been":`The situation is present, so the past perfect is wrong.`},text:`He behaves as though he ___ (be) the director, but he is only an intern.`,answers:[[`were`,`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-108`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Not once' at the start, invert the auxiliary and subject: Not once did she call.`,wrongReasons:{"he thanked":`After 'Not once' at the start, invert with 'did'.`,"has he thanked":`'during all those years' is a finished period, so the present perfect is wrong.`},text:`Not once ___ (he / thank) us for our help during all those years.`,answers:[[`did he thank`,`had he thanked`]]},{id:`c1-vc-109`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'All I want to do is + bare infinitive' focuses on one action: All I need to do is sign.`,wrongReasons:{do:`After 'want' you need the to-infinitive: 'want to do'.`,doing:`'want' is followed by the to-infinitive, not the -ing form.`},text:`All I want ___ (do) is sleep for a week.`,answers:[[`to do`]]},{id:`c1-vc-110`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A passive third-conditional result uses would have been + past participle: He would have been saved.`,wrongReasons:{"would have rescued":`The victims did not rescue anyone; a passive form is needed.`,"would be rescued":`The situation is in the past, so use 'would have been'.`},text:`The victims ___ (rescue) if the helicopter had arrived sooner.`,answers:[[`would have been rescued`,`could have been rescued`,`might have been rescued`]]},{id:`c1-vc-111`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`The clause after 'It was ... that' can be passive: It was because of the strike that trains were delayed.`,wrongReasons:{cancelled:`The flights did not cancel anything; a passive form is needed.`,"have been cancelled":`'It was' places the event in the past, so the present perfect is wrong.`},text:`It was because of the fog that the flights ___ (cancel).`,answers:[[`were cancelled`,`were canceled`,`had been cancelled`,`had been canceled`]]},{id:`c1-vc-112`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an action in progress, use the present continuous passive: The house is being painted.`,wrongReasons:{"is repaired":`'at the moment' shows an action in progress, so use 'is being repaired'.`,"is repairing":`The bridge does not repair anything; a passive form is needed.`},text:`The bridge ___ (repair) at the moment, so traffic is being diverted.`,answers:[[`is being repaired`]]},{id:`c1-vc-113`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a wish about a present ability use wish + could: I wish I could swim.`,wrongReasons:{can:`After 'I wish' use the past form 'could', not 'can'.`,"could have":`'could have' expresses a past regret, but this is about the present.`},text:`I wish I ___ (can) play a musical instrument.`,answers:[[`could`]]},{id:`c1-vc-114`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'It was not until ... that' is followed by the past simple: It was not until noon that he woke up.`,wrongReasons:{become:`The event is in the past, so use the past simple 'became'.`,"has become":`'the 1990s' is a finished time, so the present perfect is wrong.`},text:`It was not until the 1990s that the internet ___ (become) widely available.`,answers:[[`became`]]},{id:`c1-vc-115`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'So + adjective' at the start takes inversion: So loud was the music that I left.`,wrongReasons:{"the melody was":`After 'So beautiful' at the start, put the verb before the subject.`,"did the melody be":`'be' is inverted directly, without 'did'.`},text:`So beautiful ___ (the melody / be) that the audience fell silent.`,answers:[[`was the melody`]]},{id:`c1-vc-116`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'remember', use being + past participle for a passive memory: I remember being told.`,wrongReasons:{giving:`The speaker received the instructions, so a passive form is needed.`,"to be given":`'remember to' refers to a future duty, not a memory.`},text:`I don't remember ___ (give) any instructions about the deadline.`,answers:[[`being given`,`having been given`]]},{id:`c1-vc-117`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a past situation use 'if it hadn't been for' + noun: If it hadn't been for the rain, we would have won.`,wrongReasons:{"weren't":`The storm happened last night, so refer to the past with 'hadn't been'.`,"wouldn't have been":`'would' does not go in the if-clause; use the past perfect.`},text:`If it ___ (not / be) for the storm last night, the match would have gone ahead.`,answers:[[`hadn't been`,`had not been`]]},{id:`c1-vc-118`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In an 'It was ... who' cleft, the relative clause keeps the normal tense: It was Tom who called.`,wrongReasons:{suggest:`The event is in the past, so use the past simple.`,"has suggested":`'It was' sets the time in the past, so the present perfect does not fit.`},text:`It was Maria who ___ (suggest) the idea in the first place.`,answers:[[`suggested`]]},{id:`c1-vc-119`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`With 'supposing' and 'would', use the past simple for an imaginary situation: Supposing you lost your job, what would you do?`,wrongReasons:{win:`The result uses 'would', so the condition needs the past simple, not the present.`,"had won":`The question is about an imaginary future, not the past, so the past perfect is wrong.`},text:`Supposing you ___ (win) the lottery, what would you do first?`,answers:[[`won`,`were to win`]]},{id:`c1-vc-120`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`The future passive is will be + past participle: The road will be closed tomorrow.`,wrongReasons:{"will open":`'by the Health Minister' shows the wing receives the action, so a passive is needed.`,opens:`The sentence needs a passive future form, not the active present.`},text:`The new hospital wing ___ (open) by the Health Minister next month.`,answers:[[`will be opened`,`is going to be opened`,`is to be opened`,`is being opened`]]},{id:`c1-vc-121`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A negative object at the start ('Not a word') triggers inversion: Not a sound did we hear.`,wrongReasons:{"she said":`After 'Not a word' at the start, invert with 'did'.`,"said she":`Use 'did' + subject + base form, not the main verb first.`},text:`Not a word ___ (she / say) during the entire journey.`,answers:[[`did she say`,`had she said`]]},{id:`c1-vc-122`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Rules are often expressed with the present passive: Photography is not permitted.`,wrongReasons:{"doesn't allow":`Smoking does not allow anything; use the passive 'is not allowed'.`,"is not allowing":`The continuous form is wrong; rules use the present simple passive.`},text:`Smoking ___ (not / allow) anywhere on the premises.`,answers:[[`is not allowed`,`isn't allowed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-123`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional: past condition, present result: If I had trained harder, I would still be playing today.`,wrongReasons:{"would have still worked":`'today' shows a present result, so use would + infinitive.`,"will still work":`The situation is imaginary, so use 'would', not 'will'.`},text:`If the doctors had diagnosed the illness earlier, he ___ (still / work) today.`,answers:[[`would still be working`,`would still work`]]},{id:`c1-vc-124`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A 'What' clause is singular, so the verb is singular: What I want is a rest.`,wrongReasons:{are:`The what-clause is singular, so use 'is'.`,am:`The subject is the whole what-clause, not 'I', so use 'is'.`},text:`What I need right now ___ (be) a long holiday.`,answers:[[`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-125`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For a future plan in the passive, use will be + past participle: The changes will be introduced next year.`,wrongReasons:{"will implement":`A policy does not implement anything; a passive form is needed.`,implements:`The sentence refers to the future and needs a passive form.`},text:`The new policy ___ (implement) gradually over the coming months.`,answers:[[`will be implemented`,`is to be implemented`,`is going to be implemented`,`is being implemented`]]},{id:`c1-vc-126`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`An inverted condition can use Were + subject + to-infinitive: Were he to leave, we would struggle.`,wrongReasons:{"the government introduce":`After 'Were + subject' use the to-infinitive.`,"the government introduced":`The past simple does not follow 'Were + subject'; use 'to introduce'.`},text:`Were ___ (the government / introduce) the new tax, many small businesses would close.`,answers:[[`the government to introduce`]]},{id:`c1-vc-127`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use 'Having' + past participle for an earlier, completed period: Having worked there for years, he knew everyone.`,wrongReasons:{living:`The ten years abroad came before the return home, so use the perfect participle.`,lived:`'Lived' alone cannot start this clause; use 'Having lived'.`},text:`___ (live) abroad for ten years, she found it hard to readjust to life at home.`,answers:[[`Having lived`,`Having been living`]]},{id:`c1-vc-128`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'It's high time' + subject, use the past simple with present meaning: It's high time you went to bed.`,wrongReasons:{does:`'It's high time' + subject takes the past simple, not the present.`,do:`The base form is wrong here; this structure needs the past simple.`},text:`It's high time the council ___ (do) something about the potholes.`,answers:[[`did`]]},{id:`c1-vc-129`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Hardly ever' at the start, invert with an auxiliary: Hardly ever does she smile.`,wrongReasons:{"my grandfather complained":`After 'Hardly ever' at the start, invert with 'did'.`,"complained my grandfather":`Use the auxiliary 'did' before the subject, not the main verb.`},text:`Hardly ever ___ (my grandfather / complain) about his health, even when he was ill.`,answers:[[`did my grandfather complain`]]},{id:`c1-vc-130`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'If only' + past simple expresses a wish about the present: If only I knew the answer.`,wrongReasons:{have:`'If only' about the present needs the past simple.`,"had had":`'these days' refers to the present, so the past perfect is wrong.`},text:`If only I ___ (have) more time to travel these days!`,answers:[[`had`]]},{id:`c1-vc-131`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an imaginary future condition with 'wouldn't', use the past simple: Even if he asked, I wouldn't go.`,wrongReasons:{offer:`The result uses 'wouldn't', so the condition needs the past simple.`,"had offered":`The past perfect would need 'wouldn't have moved' in the result.`},text:`Even if they ___ (offer) me double the salary, I wouldn't move to that company.`,answers:[[`offered`,`were to offer`]]},{id:`c1-vc-132`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Not until' + clause, invert in the main clause: Not until he called did I relax.`,wrongReasons:{"i noticed":`After 'Not until ...' the main clause must be inverted.`,"i did notice":`The auxiliary 'did' must come before the subject.`},text:`Not until the lights came on ___ (I / notice) the stain on my shirt.`,answers:[[`did I notice`]]},{id:`c1-vc-133`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Mixed conditional: past condition (past perfect), present result: If we had acted earlier, things would be better now.`,wrongReasons:{invested:`'decades ago' refers to a completed past time, so the past perfect is needed.`,"would have invested":`'would have' does not go in the if-clause.`},text:`If we ___ (invest) in renewable energy decades ago, the climate crisis would be less severe today.`,answers:[[`had invested`]]},{id:`c1-vc-134`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'get something done' uses the past participle, also for bad experiences: She got her bag snatched.`,wrongReasons:{stole:`After 'got + object' use the past participle 'stolen', not the past simple.`,steal:`The base form is wrong; use the past participle.`},text:`He got his wallet ___ (steal) on the crowded tram.`,answers:[[`stolen`]]},{id:`c1-vc-135`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`First conditional: if + present simple, will + infinitive: If it rises, we will leave.`,wrongReasons:{"will rise":`Do not use 'will' in the if-clause of a first conditional.`,rose:`The result uses 'will', so the past simple does not fit.`},text:`If the river ___ (rise) another metre, the village will be flooded.`,answers:[[`rises`]]},{id:`c1-vc-136`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Seldom' at the start, use do/does + subject + verb: Seldom does she complain.`,wrongReasons:{"we get":`After 'Seldom' at the start, invert with 'do'.`,"get we":`Use the auxiliary 'do' before the subject, not the main verb.`},text:`Seldom ___ (we / get) the chance to see wolves in the wild these days.`,answers:[[`do we get`]]},{id:`c1-vc-137`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'Scarcely ... when' takes the past perfect with inversion: Scarcely had we arrived when it rained.`,wrongReasons:{"the plane had taken off":`After 'Scarcely' at the start, the auxiliary comes before the subject.`,"did the plane take off":`'Scarcely ... when' needs the past perfect, not the past simple.`},text:`Scarcely ___ (the plane / take off) when the engine failed.`,answers:[[`had the plane taken off`]]},{id:`c1-vc-138`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`In a future condition, use the present perfect for an action completed before another: If he has left, I'll call later.`,wrongReasons:{"will have finished":`Do not use 'will' in the if-clause; use the present perfect.`,finished:`The condition is about the future, so the past simple is wrong.`},text:`If the meeting ___ (finish) by the time I get there, I'll go straight home.`,answers:[[`has finished`,`is finished`]]},{id:`c1-vc-139`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`An unreal past condition in the passive uses had been + past participle: If it had been built properly, it wouldn't have fallen.`,wrongReasons:{"were stored":`The result is in the past, so the past perfect passive is needed.`,"had stored":`The samples do not store anything themselves, so a passive form is needed.`},text:`If the samples ___ (store) at room temperature, they would have deteriorated within hours.`,answers:[[`had been stored`]]},{id:`c1-vc-140`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`passive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`Use 'It is said that' to report a general belief: It is said that he is rich.`,wrongReasons:{says:`'It says' is used for written texts; for a general belief use 'It is said'.`,"is saying":`The continuous form is wrong; the reporting passive is 'It is said'.`},text:`It ___ (say) that the castle is haunted.`,answers:[[`is said`]]},{id:`c1-vc-141`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'What happened was (that)' introduces a past event: What happened was that I fell.`,wrongReasons:{is:`The event is in the past, so use 'was'.`,were:`The what-clause is singular, so use 'was'.`},text:`What happened ___ (be) that the server crashed during the update.`,answers:[[`was`]]},{id:`c1-vc-142`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'in case' use a present tense for a possible future event: Take an umbrella in case it rains.`,wrongReasons:{"will fail":`After 'in case' use the present simple, not 'will'.`,"would fail":`The main clause is an instruction about the future, so 'would' is wrong.`},text:`In case the power ___ (fail), keep a torch next to your bed.`,answers:[[`fails`]]},{id:`c1-vc-143`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle can shorten a passive relative clause: The coins found (= which were found) are rare.`,wrongReasons:{finding:`The documents were found by someone, so use the past participle.`,founded:`'founded' is the past of 'found' (to establish); the participle of 'find' is 'found'.`},text:`The documents ___ (find) in the attic shed new light on the family's history.`,answers:[[`found`]]},{id:`c1-vc-144`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`For an imaginary situation with 'would', use 'could' as the past of 'can': Imagine you could fly.`,wrongReasons:{can:`The situation is imaginary, so use the unreal past form 'could'.`,"could have":`'could have' refers to the past, but this is an imaginary present.`},text:`Imagine you ___ (can) live in any century. Which one would you choose?`,answers:[[`could`]]},{id:`c1-vc-145`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`cleft-sentences`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'What we should do is + bare infinitive' suggests an action: What you need to do is rest.`,wrongReasons:{are:`The what-clause is singular, so use 'is'.`,was:`The suggestion is about now, so use the present 'is'.`},text:`What we should do ___ (be) ask for a second quote.`,answers:[[`is`]]},{id:`c1-vc-146`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After an inverted third-conditional clause, use would have + past participle: Had she called, I would have answered.`,wrongReasons:{"wouldn't miss":`The situation is in the past, so use would have + past participle.`,"hadn't missed":`The result clause needs 'would have', not the past perfect.`},text:`Had we left an hour earlier, we ___ (not / miss) the ferry.`,answers:[[`wouldn't have missed`,`would not have missed`]]},{id:`c1-vc-147`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`conditionals`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`'But for' means 'if it had not been for'; with a past event use would have + past participle: But for the map, we would have got lost.`,wrongReasons:{"would drown":`The rescue happened in the past, so use would have + past participle.`,"had drowned":`The result clause needs 'would have', not the past perfect.`},text:`But for the lifeguard's quick reaction, the boy ___ (drown).`,answers:[[`would have drowned`,`might have drowned`,`could have drowned`]]},{id:`c1-vc-148`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`inversion`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'Not only' use auxiliary + subject + verb: Not only does he cook, but he also cleans.`,wrongReasons:{"she speaks":`After 'Not only' at the start, invert with 'does'.`,"speaks she":`Use the auxiliary 'does' for inversion, not the main verb.`},text:`Not only ___ (she / speak) five languages, but she also writes poetry.`,answers:[[`does she speak`]]},{id:`c1-vc-149`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`subjunctive`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`After 'demand that' use the bare subjunctive: They demanded that he leave.`,wrongReasons:{refunds:`The subjunctive does not take -s.`,"will refund":`'will' is not used after 'demand that'; use the base form.`},text:`She demanded that the company ___ (refund) the full amount.`,answers:[[`refund`,`should refund`]]},{id:`c1-vc-150`,type:`verb-conjugate`,level:`C1`,topic:`participle-clauses`,prompt:`Write the correct form of the verb in brackets.`,explanation:`A past participle clause expresses a passive idea: Viewed from the hill, the town looks tiny.`,wrongReasons:{seeing:`The islands are seen, they do not see, so use the past participle.`,"having seen":`'Having seen' is active and would mean the islands saw something.`},text:`___ (see) from above, the islands look like scattered emeralds.`,answers:[[`Seen`]]}]};export{e as default};